  <section id="trip-length">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reality Check</p>
    <h2>Short trips aren&rsquo;t half price</h2>
    <p>The short escapes exist because a first Europe trip with the kids feels like a big swing. But the flights are the expensive part &mdash; roughly $4.5&ndash;5k for the four of us &mdash; and that cost is identical whether we stay 7 nights or 12. Cutting nights only trims the cheap part of the trip.</p>
    <div class="lm-legend"><span><i class="lm-short"></i>7-night escape</span><span><i></i>Full 12-night trip</span><span><i style="background:#d5cdbe"></i>Jet-lag adjustment day</span></div>
    <div class="lm-grid">
      <div class="lm-card">
        <h3>Same destination, same airfare</h3>
        <p class="lm-sub">Portugal head-to-head: mid-range planning total for the family of 4.</p>
        <div class="lm-row" title="Short Portugal: $8.7k&ndash;$12.0k planning band">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>Short Portugal &middot; 7 nights</span><b>$10.3k</b></div>
          <div class="lm-bar lm-short" style="width:94%"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lm-row" title="Full Portugal: $7.5k&ndash;$11.7k planning band">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>Full Portugal &middot; 12 nights</span><b>$9.6k</b></div>
          <div class="lm-bar" style="width:87%"></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lm-note"><b>The 12-night trip costs less.</b> Five fewer nights, higher total &mdash; because the airfare doesn&rsquo;t shrink when the trip does.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lm-card">
        <h3>What one night actually costs</h3>
        <p class="lm-sub">Mid-range total &divide; nights, family of 4.</p>
        <div class="lm-row" title="Full Portugal: $9.6k over 12 nights">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>Full Portugal</span><b>$800</b></div>
          <div class="lm-bar" style="width:50%"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lm-row" title="Median of the 21 ranked two-week plans">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>Typical full trip</span><b>$1,130</b></div>
          <div class="lm-bar" style="width:71%"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lm-row" title="Puerto Rico, Acadia, Azores, Iceland, Madeira average">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>Short domestic / Atlantic</span><b>$1,140</b></div>
          <div class="lm-bar lm-short" style="width:71%"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lm-row" title="Algarve, Portugal, Sicily, Ischia escapes average">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>Short Mediterranean</span><b>$1,490</b></div>
          <div class="lm-bar lm-short" style="width:93%"></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lm-note"><b>Going long is the value play.</b> Stretching a Mediterranean escape to a typical full trip adds ~$3.2k for 5 more nights &mdash; about <b>$640 a night</b>, the cheapest nights we can buy in Europe.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lm-card">
        <h3>Jet lag takes the same bite</h3>
        <p class="lm-sub">Kids new to Europe need ~2 days to adjust &mdash; on any length of trip.</p>
        <div class="lm-row">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>7-night escape</span><b>5 good days</b></div>
          <div class="lm-days"><i class="lm-day lm-lost"></i><i class="lm-day lm-lost"></i><i class="lm-day lm-short"></i><i class="lm-day lm-short"></i><i class="lm-day lm-short"></i><i class="lm-day lm-short"></i><i class="lm-day lm-short"></i></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lm-row">
          <div class="lm-row-top"><span>12-night trip</span><b>10 good days</b></div>
          <div class="lm-days"><i class="lm-day lm-lost"></i><i class="lm-day lm-lost"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i><i class="lm-day"></i></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lm-note"><b>Same adjustment cost, double the payoff.</b> A 7-night Europe trip pays full airfare for about 5 fully-enjoyed days; 12 nights pays the same airfare for 10.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lm-lab">
      <div class="lm-lab-left">
        <h3>Find the sweet spot</h3>
        <p class="lm-sub">Drag the nights. Live model for a warm-Europe trip, family of 4: flights + transfers <b>$4.5&ndash;5k fixed</b>, plus <b>$600&ndash;800 per night</b> on the ground. Estimates only &mdash; the trip pages&rsquo; audited budgets stay the source of truth.</p>
        <div class="lm-slider-row">
          <input type="range" id="lm-nights" min="5" max="14" step="1" value="12" aria-label="Trip length in nights">
          <output id="lm-nights-out" for="lm-nights">12 nights</output>
        </div>
        <div class="lm-tiles" aria-live="polite">
          <div class="lm-tile"><span>Est. total</span><b id="lm-total">&nbsp;</b></div>
          <div class="lm-tile"><span>Per night</span><b id="lm-pernight">&nbsp;</b></div>
          <div class="lm-tile"><span>Good days</span><b id="lm-good">&nbsp;</b></div>
          <div class="lm-tile"><span>Est. PTO</span><b id="lm-pto">&nbsp;</b></div>
          <div class="lm-tile"><span>Nights score</span><b id="lm-nscore">&nbsp;</b></div>
          <div class="lm-tile"><span>Score vs 12n plan</span><b id="lm-delta">&nbsp;</b></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lm-lab-verdict" id="lm-verdict-line">&nbsp;</p>
        <p class="lm-lab-note">Not modeled: a shorter total can lift the double-weighted Budget axis for plans above the $15k line &mdash; that case is what per-trip variants are for.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lm-lab-right">
        <p class="lm-chart-title">Cost per <b>good</b> day (after the 2 jet-lag days) &mdash; watch it flatten</p>
        <svg id="lm-curve" viewBox="0 0 340 224" role="img" aria-label="Cost per good day falls steeply from 5 to 11 nights, then flattens near 12 to 14 nights"></svg>
      </div>
    </div>
    <script>
    (function(){
      var slider=document.getElementById('lm-nights');
      var svg=document.getElementById('lm-curve');
      if(!slider||!svg)return;
      var FLO=4500,FHI=5000,NLO=600,NHI=800,NMIN=5,NMAX=14;
      function model(n){
        var lo=FLO+NLO*n,hi=FHI+NHI*n,mid=(lo+hi)/2;
        var nscore=n>=12?5:(n===11?4:(n===10?3:(n===9?2:1)));
        return{lo:lo,hi:hi,mid:mid,good:n-2,nscore:nscore,pto:Math.round((n+1)*8/13),perNight:mid/n,perGood:mid/(n-2)};
      }
      var PX0=44,PX1=326,PY0=14,PY1=192,YMIN=1100,YMAX=2900;
      function X(n){return PX0+(n-NMIN)/(NMAX-NMIN)*(PX1-PX0);}
      function Y(v){return PY1-(v-YMIN)/(YMAX-YMIN)*(PY1-PY0);}
      function el(tag,attrs,text){
        var e=document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg',tag);
        for(var k in attrs)e.setAttribute(k,attrs[k]);
        if(text)e.textContent=text;
        svg.appendChild(e);return e;
      }
      el('rect',{x:X(11),y:PY0,width:X(12.6)-X(11),height:PY1-PY0,fill:'#00939e',opacity:'.08'});
      el('text',{x:(X(11)+X(12.6))/2,y:PY0+12,'text-anchor':'middle',fill:'#00737c','font-size':'9','font-weight':'800','letter-spacing':'.08em'},'SWEET SPOT');
      [1500,2000,2500].forEach(function(v){
        el('line',{x1:PX0,y1:Y(v),x2:PX1,y2:Y(v),stroke:'#e3dccc','stroke-width':'1'});
        el('text',{x:PX0-6,y:Y(v)+3,'text-anchor':'end',fill:'#8d8676','font-size':'9'},'$'+(v/1000).toFixed(1)+'k');
      });
      var pts=[];
      for(var n=NMIN;n<=NMAX;n++){pts.push(X(n)+','+Y(model(n).perGood));}
      el('polyline',{points:pts.join(' '),fill:'none',stroke:'#00939e','stroke-width':'2','stroke-linejoin':'round'});
      for(n=NMIN;n<=NMAX;n++){
        el('circle',{cx:X(n),cy:Y(model(n).perGood),r:'2.5',fill:'#00939e'});
        el('text',{x:X(n),y:PY1+14,'text-anchor':'middle',fill:'#8d8676','font-size':'9'},n);
      }
      el('text',{x:(PX0+PX1)/2,y:PY1+26,'text-anchor':'middle',fill:'#8d8676','font-size':'9','font-weight':'700'},'NIGHTS');
      var marker=el('circle',{r:'6',fill:'#1a1712',stroke:'#fffdf8','stroke-width':'2'});
      var markerLabel=el('text',{'text-anchor':'middle',fill:'#1a1712','font-size':'11','font-weight':'800'});
      function fmtK(v){return '$'+(v/1000).toFixed(1)+'k';}
      function fmt(v){return '$'+Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-US');}
      function verdictFor(n){
        if(n<=8)return 'Worst-value zone: full airfare for '+(n-2)+' good days. This is the math the short Europe escapes pay — fine domestic, expensive across the Atlantic.';
        if(n<=10)return 'The middle ground saves ~$'+((model(12).mid-model(n).mid)/1000).toFixed(1)+'k vs 12 nights but drops the Nights score to '+model(n).nscore+'/5. Only worth it if the trim pulls a too-expensive plan under the $15k line.';
        if(n<=12)return 'Sweet spot: the airfare is fully amortized, Nights scores '+model(n).nscore+'/5, and the curve is flat — each extra night now costs only ~$700.';
        return 'Diminishing returns: cost per good day barely falls, estimated PTO climbs to '+model(n).pto+' days, and the Jun 24–26 Pittsburgh commitment caps how far this stretches.';
      }
      function set(id,v){document.getElementById(id).textContent=v;}
      function update(){
        var n=+slider.value,m=model(n);
        set('lm-nights-out',n+' nights');
        set('lm-total',fmtK(m.lo)+'–'+fmtK(m.hi));
        set('lm-pernight',fmt(m.perNight));
        set('lm-good',m.good+' of '+n);
        set('lm-pto',m.pto+' days');
        set('lm-nscore',m.nscore+'/5');
        set('lm-delta',(m.nscore===5?'±0':(m.nscore-5))+' /55');
        set('lm-verdict-line',verdictFor(n));
        var mx=X(n),my=Y(m.perGood);
        marker.setAttribute('cx',mx);marker.setAttribute('cy',my);
        markerLabel.setAttribute('x',Math.min(Math.max(mx,PX0+24),PX1-24));
        markerLabel.setAttribute('y',my-11);
        markerLabel.textContent=fmt(m.perGood);
      }
      slider.addEventListener('input',update);
      update();
    })();
    </script>
    <div class="lm-verdict">
      <h3>The verdict</h3>
      <div class="lm-verdict-grid">
        <p><b>Book the full 12 nights.</b> Portugal&rsquo;s 12-night plan is the cheapest complete plan on the whole board &mdash; cheaper than most 7-night escapes. Going long is the budget move, not the splurge.</p>
        <p><b>8&ndash;10 nights isn&rsquo;t a magic middle.</b> Trimming to 10 nights saves only about $1&ndash;1.5k and 2 PTO days. What actually protects a first Europe trip with kids is fewer bases and fewer connections &mdash; pick a calm 2&ndash;3 base plan, not a shorter one.</p>
        <p><b>When short does make sense: cheap flights.</b> Puerto Rico, Acadia, and the Azores land near $8k because getting there is cheap &mdash; they&rsquo;re the escapes that don&rsquo;t burn a $5k airfare on a 7-night stay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="short-trips">
    <div class="short-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">New · 7 Nights or Less</p>
      <h2>Short, easy escapes</h2>
      <p>Smaller-budget trips built around fewer bases, lighter logistics, and enough breathing room to feel like a vacation. Warm water is a bonus here, not the price of admission.</p>
      <p class="short-method"><b>Ranked only against each other:</b> budget and ease count double; weather, fire safety, swimming, variety, food, risk, and PTO count once. Ties favor fewer PTO days, then the lower budget ceiling.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="short-grid">
      {%- for trip in shortTrips %}
      <a class="short-card" href="{{ trip.href }}">
        <div class="short-photo"><img src="{{ trip.heroImage }}" alt="{{ trip.heroAlt }}" loading="lazy"><span class="short-badge">#{{ trip.shortRank }} · {{ trip.pto.nights }} nights</span><span class="short-score">{{ trip.shortScore }}/55</span></div>
        <div class="short-body">
          <span class="short-dates">{{ trip.travelWindow[0] | displayDate }}–{{ trip.travelWindow[1] | displayDate }}</span>
          <h3>{{ trip.displayName }}</h3>
          <p>{{ trip.blurb }}</p>
          <p class="short-verdict">{{ trip.shortVerdict }}</p>
          <div class="short-stats">
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Family budget</span><b>${{ (trip.budget.floorUsd / 1000) | round(1) }}k–${{ (trip.budget.ceilUsd / 1000) | round(1) }}k</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>PTO</span><b>{{ trip.pto.days }} days</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Home bases</span><b>{% if trip.metrics.baseMoves != null %}{{ trip.metrics.baseMoves + 1 }}{% else %}Minimal{% endif %}</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Swimming</span><b>{% if trip.facets.swimType == 'geothermal' %}Warm geothermal{% elif trip.facets.swimType == 'warm-sea-plus-thermal' %}{{ trip.facets.swimTempF[1] }}°F sea + thermal{% elif trip.facets.heatedSwimTempF %}Pool + Atlantic{% else %}{{ trip.facets.swimTempF[0] }}–{{ trip.facets.swimTempF[1] }}°F water{% endif %}</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Fire disruption</span><b>{{ trip.fireRisk.level }} · {{ trip.fireRisk.chanceBand }}</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="short-ready">{{ trip.readiness.label }} →</div>
        </div>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="fire-risk">
    <p class="eyebrow">New decision factor</p>
    <h2>Wildfire disruption by location and season</h2>
    <p>These bands estimate the chance that fire, smoke, evacuation, road or park closures, or related flight disruption materially changes the itinerary during its exact dates. They are conservative planning estimates inferred from official recent evidence and fire history—not promises or actuarial forecasts. Each trip takes the least-safe score among its route segments.</p>
    <div class="rubric-note"><b>Higher is safer:</b> 5 = very low (&lt;2%); 4 = low (2&ndash;5%); 3 = moderate (5&ndash;10%); 2 = high (10&ndash;20%); 1 = very high (&gt;20%). Recheck official daily danger maps and active incidents 14 days, 72 hours, and each morning before rural drives or hikes. A live red/extreme warning overrides the historical band.</div>
    <div class="matrix-wrap"><table class="budget-tbl"><thead><tr><th>Location and trip window</th><th>Planning chance</th><th>Safety score</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      {%- for id, profile in fireRisk.profiles %}
      <tr><td><b>{{ profile.name }}</b></td><td>{% if profile.score == 5 %}Very low · &lt;2%{% elif profile.score == 4 %}Low · 2&ndash;5%{% elif profile.score == 3 %}Moderate · 5&ndash;10%{% elif profile.score == 2 %}High · 10&ndash;20%{% else %}Very high · &gt;20%{% endif %}</td><td><b>{{ profile.score }}/5</b></td><td>{{ profile.rationale }}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section id="trips" class="shortlist">
    <div class="sl-head">
      <p class="sl-eyebrow">Trip Shortlist</p>
      <h2>Twenty-one ranked ways to spend the same two weeks</h2>
      <p>Ranked by the scoreboard — pure data, no preference thumb on the scale; the top score is outlined in red. Tap any card for the full day-by-day itinerary. Nights pill = hotel (bed) nights; the <b>+1</b> chip is the red-eye/travel night away.</p>
    </div>
    {% include "hub/cards.njk" %}
  </section>

  <section id="decision">
    <p class="eyebrow">Decision Console</p>
    <h2>Choose the priority</h2>
    <p>The default ranking uses Budget at double weight plus Weather, Fire safety, Swim, Variety, Ease, Food, Risk, Nights, and Novelty; PTO is displayed and available for custom weighting. Fire safety is the evidence-based planning chance that wildfire, smoke, evacuation, or closures materially disrupt the exact route during its exact dates. Scores remain provisional where exact 2027 schedules, complete quote sets, or next-season fire conditions are still unverified. Nine trips are excluded by family decision: <b>Albania</b>, <b>Balkans</b>, <b>California</b>, <b>Canary Islands</b>, <b>Croatia</b>, <b>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</b>, <b>Southern France</b>, <b>Spain</b>, and <b>Turkish Riviera</b>. Click a row to highlight that trip in the scoreboard.</p>
    <div class="matrix-wrap">
      <table class="decision-table"><thead><tr><th>If you're optimizing for&hellip;</th><th>Winner</th><th>Runner-up</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr class="decision-row on" data-priority="balanced" data-trip="portugal"><td><b>Best Overall On The Data</b></td><td>Portugal</td><td>Madeira + Mallorca</td><td>Portugal leads at 43/55 because its reconciled $7.5k&ndash;11.7k range stays below the $12k target while preserving 12 nights and three bases. Madeira + Mallorca is #2 at 41/55 with warmer water, stronger contrast, and an $11.8k&ndash;14.8k within-preference band.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="hiking" data-trip="madeira-mallorca"><td><b>Best Epic Scenery + Hiking</b></td><td>Madeira + Mallorca</td><td>Madeira + Crete</td><td>Madeira's Arieiro&ndash;Ruivo ridge, levadas, and Porto Moniz are the strongest scenery/hiking week on the board; among the Madeira hybrids, Mallorca is the only version whose audited high case stays under the $15k preferred maximum. Madeira + Crete keeps the same hiking week but reaches $16.8k.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="bestofboth" data-trip="portugal-crete"><td><b>Best of Both, Calmest Version</b></td><td>Portugal + Crete</td><td>Portugal + Sicily</td><td>The mainland openers are the low-drama hybrids: no FNC wind risk, fewer legs, lower floors. Crete wins on cost/simplicity (3 bases, 8 PTO); Sicily wins on the full Cefalu&ndash;Ortigia&ndash;Taormina sweep but carries fragile air.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="pure" data-trip="hawaii"><td><b>Best Warm Water Overall</b></td><td>Hawaii</td><td>Maui + Kauai</td><td>Both Hawaii routes deliver 78&ndash;81&deg;F Pacific water and score 5/5 for swimming. Oʻahu + Hawaiʻi Island ranks higher because it uses two fewer PTO days and its $11k&ndash;15.8k band is far below Maui + Kauai's premium $14.6k&ndash;21.6k range.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="value" data-trip="portugal"><td><b>Best Value</b></td><td>Portugal</td><td>Spain</td><td>Portugal is the cheapest complete ranked route ($7.5k&ndash;11.7k) and the only full band below target. Spain's $8.8k&ndash;14.8k band is the next within-preference value case, though its unitemized contingency and nine PTO days keep it well behind Portugal.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="europe" data-trip="sardinia"><td><b>Best Europe If Novelty Matters</b></td><td>Sardinia &amp; Corsica</td><td>Sicily &amp; Malta</td><td>Both are 5/5-novelty Italy-family routes at ordinary June Mediterranean temperatures (72&ndash;75&deg;F, swim 3); Sardinia/Corsica pairs that with dramatic limestone coves but reaches $16.8k. Sicily &amp; Malta adds Etna and Malta lagoons with a $15.8k high case. Salento-Amalfi is less novel because Capri and the Puglia towns repeat prior travel.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="warm-europe" data-trip="turkey"><td><b>Best Warm-Water Europe-Style Trip</b></td><td>Turkish Riviera</td><td>Portugal + Crete</td><td>Turkey has the warmest non-Hawaii sea on the board (75&ndash;79&deg;F, swim 5), but it is excluded by family decision and also carries June heat, a scoped advisory, and a ~$17.4k high case. Portugal + Crete is the ranked alternative, with Crete's 73&ndash;74&deg;F sea and a lower planning high.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="italy" data-trip="italy"><td><b>Best Italy Option</b></td><td>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</td><td>Sardinia &amp; Corsica</td><td>Salento/Maratea/Amalfi has the strongest food and route variety, plus the warmer swim (Amalfi/Capri, swim 4 vs Sardinia/Corsica's swim 3); Sardinia/Corsica counters with dramatic limestone coves and a short Corsica ferry.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="swim" data-trip="hawaii"><td><b>Best Swim Overall</b></td><td>Hawaii</td><td>Maui + Kauai</td><td>The two ranked Hawaii routes are the board's clearest warm-water choices. Maui + Kauai adds three hotel nights and stronger scenery, while the existing Hawaii plan wins the tie-break on PTO and price.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="food" data-trip="italy"><td><b>Best Picky-Eater Food</b></td><td>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</td><td>Sicily &amp; Malta</td><td>Sicily/Malta is extremely safe for plain food, but the simpler three-base route nudges Italy ahead; both cross the preferred maximum without clean quotes.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="history" data-trip="spain"><td><b>Best Architecture &amp; History</b></td><td>Spain</td><td>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</td><td>Spain still concentrates the strongest Alhambra/Mezquita/Alcazar package; Italy counters with Herculaneum, Lecce, Amalfi, and Capri.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="domestic" data-trip="california"><td><b>Best Domestic Road Trip</b></td><td>California Pacific Coast</td><td>Hawaii</td><td>California would win if passport-free mainland driving is the brief, but it is excluded by family decision (kept here for reference). Hawaii is the closest ranked no-passport alternative, though it's a beach trip, not a road trip.</td></tr>
        <tr class="decision-row" data-priority="adventure" data-trip="turkey"><td><b>Most Adventurous</b></td><td>Turkish Riviera</td><td>Balkans</td><td>Both are excluded references: Balkans has the biggest frontier feel, while Turkey has the cleaner three-base adventure-lite route.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="scoreboard">
    <p class="eyebrow">Scoreboard</p>
    <h2>Fast read on the tradeoffs</h2>
    <div class="rubric-note"><b>How these scores work:</b> Budget is weighted <b>double</b> against your $12k target / $15k strongly preferred maximum; Weather, <b>Fire safety</b>, Swim, Variety, Ease, Food, Risk, <b>Nights</b>, and <b>Novelty</b> are each rated 1-5 once. Total is out of 55 (PTO is tracked as data but not part of the default total). Fire safety is higher-is-safer: 5 = &lt;2%, 4 = 2&ndash;5%, 3 = 5&ndash;10%, 2 = 10&ndash;20%, and 1 = &gt;20% planning chance of a material wildfire disruption during the exact dates. The bands combine official recent evidence, fire history, seasonality, route exposure, and itinerary flexibility; they are not actuarial forecasts. Live warnings always override them. <b>Nights</b> rewards trip length: 12+ nights &rarr; 5, 11 &rarr; 4, 10 &rarr; 3, 9 &rarr; 2, 8 or fewer &rarr; 1. <b>Novelty</b> scores route overlap against places already visited. Card order follows this table; default ties prefer a range within the budget preference, then fewer PTO days, then lower budget ceiling and floor. Cost never removes an itinerary. Explicit family exclusions stay visible but unranked.</div>
    <div class="score-legend"><span class="good"><i></i>Green = preferred / strong</span><span class="mixed"><i></i>Amber = workable tradeoff</span><span class="weak"><i></i>Rust = weak fit</span></div>
    <div id="scenario-panel" class="scenario-panel" hidden></div>
    <div id="filter-bar" class="filter-bar" hidden></div>
    <div id="weight-panel" class="weight-panel" hidden></div>
    <div id="compare-bar" class="compare-bar" hidden></div>
    <div class="matrix-wrap"><table class="compare-table scoreboard"><thead><tr><th data-sort="trip">Trip</th><th data-sort="budget">Budget (&times;2)</th><th data-sort="weather">Weather</th><th data-sort="fireRisk">Fire safety</th><th data-sort="swim">Swim</th><th data-sort="variety">Variety</th><th data-sort="ease">Ease</th><th data-sort="food">Food</th><th data-sort="risk">Risk</th><th data-sort="nights">Nights</th><th data-sort="novelty">Novelty</th><th data-sort="pto">PTO</th><th data-sort="total">Total /55</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% include "hub/scoreboard.njk" %}
</tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section id="length">
    <p class="eyebrow">Length Verdicts</p>
    <h2>Where the days are doing real work</h2>
    <div class="budget-scroll"><table class="budget-tbl length-table"><tr><th>Trip</th><th>Length verdict</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Portugal</b></td><td>12 nights is right.</td><td>Three bases stay calm; the cold-water issue does not improve enough by cutting or stretching the route.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Madeira + Crete</b></td><td>13 nights away / 12 hotel nights is right.</td><td>Four Funchal nights buy two weather shots at a clear Arieiro summit; the Lisbon buffer night is wind insurance, not a base; Chania 5 + Rethymno 2 is the honest squeeze it costs.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Madeira + Sicily</b></td><td>13 nights away / 12 hotel nights, and it is maxed out.</td><td>Five Funchal nights plus the Tuesday LIS-PMO hinge force Sicily down to six nights and two bases; there is no room left to re-add Ortigia without breaking the budget or the calendar.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Portugal + Crete</b></td><td>13 nights away / 12 hotel nights is right.</td><td>Five Portugal + seven Crete nights is the honest balance: Cascais 5, Chania 4, Rethymno 3. It keeps the signature Crete water days and one realistic gorge without reducing Portugal to a stopover.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Portugal + Sicily</b></td><td>12 hotel nights is right, but it is the busiest 12.</td><td>Five Portugal + seven Sicily nights across three bases is the max before transfer days start crowding out beach days; do not add a fourth base.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Hawaii</b></td><td>9 hotel nights plus red-eye is tight but efficient.</td><td>One more hotel night improves comfort but pushes harder against the preferred maximum.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Maui + Kauai</b></td><td>12 hotel nights is the minimum fair version.</td><td>Five Kīhei, four Poʻipū and three Princeville nights preserve a Hāna recovery day and keep western and northern Kauai drives rational; do not add a third island.</td></tr>
