      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Epic scenery + hiking</h3><p><b>Madeira + Mallorca</b> &mdash; the same Arieiro-above-the-clouds, 25 Fontes, Porto Moniz week, paired with a Mediterranean swim that keeps the whole trip under the $15k preferred maximum. <b>Madeira + Crete</b> and <b>Madeira + Sicily</b> offer the same hiking but both now cross the preferred maximum.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Pure score</h3><p><b>Portugal</b> leads at 43/55, followed by <b>Madeira + Mallorca</b> at 41/55. <b>Portugal + Sicily</b>, <b>Slovenia + Adriatic</b>, and <b>Iceland + Ischia/Cilento</b> are tied at 39/55. The Hawaii routes tie at 35/55; Oʻahu + Hawaiʻi Island ranks #15 on lower PTO and cost, while Maui + Kauai is #21 with a $21.6k high case.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Best Italy reference</h3><p><b>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</b> has the best food/variety stretch, but remains excluded by family decision and budget-gated.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Warm-water Europe</h3><p><b>Turkish Riviera</b> has the warmest non-Hawaii sea on the board (75&ndash;79&deg;F) and a clean three-base AYT-to-DLM route. It is an excluded reference at 36/55 because heat, moderate June fire exposure, long-haul airfare, the scoped advisory, and a ~$17.4k high case offset the swim advantage.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Best Europe value</h3><p><b>Croatia</b> wins value on paper ($8.4k&ndash;12.8k) but is excluded &mdash; 2026 repeat, novelty 1/5. <b>Portugal</b> is the ranked value winner because its complete $7.5k&ndash;11.7k planning band stays below target.</p></article>
