        <li><strong>Albania</strong> (Accursed Mountains: Theth/Valbona + the Riviera: Ksamil) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, 39/55, excluded by family decision</span> The best <em>warm-sea + novel</em> pick: alpine drama + Caribbean-clear swimming, cheap, one-country ground transport, no island-hop trap.</li>
        <li><strong>Madeira + Mallorca</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, #2 (41/55)</span> The Madeira ridge-hiking week paired with a sandy Mediterranean swim in Mallorca instead of a second Atlantic or Greek leg &mdash; the only Madeira hybrid whose audited high case stays within the preferred maximum.</li>
        <li><strong>Dolomites + Venice + Sardinia</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, ranked #12 (37/55)</span> Best pure epic-hiking (Tre Cime, Seceda) with a Venice opener and an epic-beach Sardinia finale. Landlocked hiking half = the variety.</li>
        <li><strong>Iceland</strong> (Reykjavík + Golden Circle + South Coast + Jökuls&aacute;rl&oacute;n) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, #6 on the data (38/55)</span> The most novel-looking option &mdash; nothing like the Med board or Mexico. Swim = warm geothermal lagoons, not the (cold) sea.</li>
